Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] radv/darwin: ASIC profile, default gfx1200 (Navi 44,
 RX 9060 XT)

The Darwin backend was hardwired to the gfx1201 canned record and PCI id
0x7550 (Navi 48). Add ac_darwin_asic.h, a compile-time profile used by
ac_darwin_drm.c (canned record) and radv_physical_device.c (PCI identity):
default gfx1200 / 0x7590 "AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT", -DRADV_DARWIN_NAVI48 for
the previous gfx1201 / 0x7550 behaviour.

Add a gfx1200 canned record to amdgpu_devices.c with the values read from a
real RX 9060 XT under Linux amdgpu (2 SE, 32 CU, 8 RB, 128-bit GDDR6, 32 MiB
MALL). cpu_accessible_vram stays at 256 MiB like the gfx1201 record: on macOS
the kext's QueryInfo overrides the heaps, so the canned value only matters
for RADV_DARWIN_MOCK and drm-shim.

Checked on Linux: drm-shim (AMDGPU_GPU_ID=gfx1200) vulkaninfo matches the
real card's shader-core properties; ac_darwin_drm.c and the Darwin block of
radv_physical_device.c pass -fsyntax-only with both profiles.
